ADDITIONAL NOTICE FOR THIS PROJECT

This Software is sample and demonstration code, published as a reference for
building on AR smart glasses. It is not a finished consumer product.

IT MIRRORS EVERYTHING. Screen capture does not distinguish between a map and
a banking app. Whatever is on the phone — notifications, messages, passwords
as they are typed, one-time codes, anything shoulder-surfable — is encoded
and sent to the glasses while mirroring runs. Stop the capture before doing
anything you would not want on the display.

THE LINK IS NOT ENCRYPTED BY THIS SOFTWARE. The video, audio and control
stream travel over a plain TCP socket on the local network, or over a Wi-Fi
Direct group whose network name and passphrase are FIXED CONSTANTS IN THIS
SOURCE and therefore public. Anyone in radio range running this code can join
that group. Change both constants before relying on it, and treat the link as
readable by anyone on the same network.

IT CAN OPERATE THE PHONE. The companion app holds an accessibility service so
the glasses can tap, scroll and type. Anything reaching that channel can act
on the phone as though a person were holding it.

THE PAGE AGENT SENDS YOUR SCREEN OFF-DEVICE. When an errand runs, a JPEG of
the mirrored phone screen is uploaded to a model provider (Google Gemini, or
Groq for speech) using your own API key, and is handled under that
provider's terms rather than these. The feature is inert until you supply a
key, but while it runs the contents of your screen leave your devices.

AWARENESS. This drives a display worn over the eyes. Do not use it while
driving or operating machinery, and stay alert to your surroundings. Use is
entirely at your own risk.
